  "title": "# Console commands over API, MCP and CLI (Urgent, Opus) Brett Nov 3 2026 07:16 ET (voice): add cons…",
  "asked": "# Console commands over API, MCP and CLI (Urgent, Opus) Brett Nov 3 2026 07:16 ET (voice): add console commands to the MCP, the API and the CLI so he can tell Amber (a Claude session) to load screens for him. Based on claude/token-control (control@1 contract, PR #246). A sibling build `token-control-opus` (branch claude/token-control-opus) is building the token/AmberX/planner API, MCP and CLI right now: fetch it and build on its server/MCP/CLI layout if it exists, and merge origin/main + that branch before the PR. Don't duplicate its work. Do: 1. control@1 `console` namespace: open a view/screen (by id, title or search), open a dialog, open a settings tab/sub-tab, run any registered action, go back, list available screens/actions (so Claude can find the right one). 2. Live delivery: the open console in Brett's browser receives the command and navigates right away (reuse Watch live / `axf focus` channel if it fits; one target per signed-in user, all his open consoles or the most recent). Also Molly and AmberX web if the same runtime makes it cheap; say in the PR what's covered. 3. REST API endpoints, MCP tools (registered through axHub so this voice/Claude session can call them), and CLI: `axf console open <screen>`, `axf console action <id>`, `axf console list`. 4. Safety: navigation and opening only; running an action that changes data needs the same approval policy as the action itself. 5. Tests, check-theme/check-controls, help pack, interactive docs entries, UI Review shots if anything visible changes. Rules: one session, no sub-agents. Tokens only (--fx-*), framework controls, no var() fallbacks. Add a THREADS.md row (profile urgent) and update each step. Commit + push branch claude/console-commands often; open the PR at the end (push banner merges it). In the PR, say exactly which axHub tool names a Claude session calls to load a screen. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, patches-web, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once.",
